                  A real run copies them into <state>/adoption-inventory.
[!!] Existing     Vector is already running here: vector.service (pid 812). Setup won't take it over, and the agent manages exactly one JSON file, so adopting it would drop what these load:
                  Vector loads 2 configuration files: <conf>/10-sources.yaml, <conf>/20-sinks.yaml.
                  Merge what it loads into one JSON file at <managed> (the Help center's Connect a device page, under Keep an existing workload, shows how), or adopt it as it is: the agent then manages only <managed>; what it loads stays where it is and no Vector started by Vectory reads it. Either way, stop it (for example: sudo systemctl disable --now vector.service), then run this command again with --adopt-existing.
